Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 03:51:23 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] fix(cron): a manual run's notice shows only the output that
 run saved

The completion notice of a background cronjob(action='run') attached the job's newest output file. A cancelled or crashed run saves none, so its notice showed the previous completed run's report (its Run Time, Run Context and file path) as this run's output. The notice now takes only a file written at or after the run's dispatch time, and says "Job output: none saved by this run." when there is none.
